// Consumer half of the intel factory: read the intel node's
// ocsf.OSINT_Inventory_Info lookup table into this node's ocsf-osint
// context. The factory appends the collection's current state on every
// walk, so the loader applies updates in event-time order (the
// indicator's STIX modified time, ORDER BY server-side): per key, the
// newest version lands last, and a revoked row (status Removed; STIX
// versioning bumps modified on revoke) erases the key after every older
// active copy re-applied it. Expired indicators (osint.expiration_time
// in the past) erase the key regardless of order.
//
// SHAPE CONTRACT (see the intel node README and the DDL comment in
// ../../../clickhouse/config/10-startup-scripts.xml): the vendored
// stix::ocsf::map emits `osint` as a one-element ARRAY, so the table's
// original dotted typed columns could never bind it — all osint.* typed
// columns sat NULL on every row while the whole array rode the
// tenzir:catch_all `event` JSON. The DDL now stores exactly that shape,
// and this loader reads via SQL-mode projection instead of table mode:
// 6.19.1 table mode does not reconstruct catch-alls at all, and 6.20
// table mode reconstructs but re-types IP-shaped indicator values,
// breaking the string keys the vendored update_context/enrich pair pins.

every 24h {
  from_clickhouse sql="SELECT `time`, `status_id`, JSONExtractArrayRaw(toString(event), 'osint') AS osint, nullIf(JSONExtractString(toString(event), 'status'), '') AS status FROM ocsf.OSINT_Inventory_Info ORDER BY `time` ASC",
    host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
    port=9000,
    user="tenzir",
    password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
    tls=false
  // The projection hands back the array elements as JSON text; re-type
  // them to the map's original record shape. parse_json's inference
  // reproduces the map's time-typed fields; its one over-inference — IP-
  // and subnet-shaped indicator values — is coerced back to the string
  // keys the vendored operators pin.
  osint = osint.map(x => parse_json(x)).map(x => merge(x, {value: string(x.value?)}))
  // Compound or non-comparison patterns yield no indicator value: such
  // entries can never join events, so drop them instead of storing
  // null-key context entries.
  where osint?[0]?.value? != null
  // The round trip rebuilds the event fields but not the schema name;
  // update_context gates on it, so stamp it back.
  @name = "ocsf.osint_inventory_info"
  tenzir::osint::update_context max_age=30d
}
